From 3a1ae2fc50ec91a7b090d969e8d0a49eb3c75083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:42:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] input: the light-gun probe - a probe press makes the game
 flash, the real press follows with the aim from that flash

House of the Dead (the Model2C core, name Model2A) flashes for one field after the
trigger and reads the gun at the end of it. Measured 2026-10-23: in a dark scene
the GunCon 2's one lit report of that flash reaches the app 33..35 ms after the
pull, after the game has read; the gun reports a field only once it has ended, so
the shot cannot be given the aim from its own flash.

With only the game's own flash and nothing changed in the core: on a pull the
physical trigger is held back and the aim goes off the screen; a probe press is
given (the game flashes and, with the gun off the screen, counts a reload); the
first valid reading after the probe press is where the gun saw that flash; the
probe press is released, the aim set, and once the game has seen the trigger up
(35 ms) the real press is given with the aim already in place. No light within
100 ms of the probe press means the gun is off the screen and the probe press
was the reload. Costs: a reload with every shot, two flashes, the shot reaches
the game about 80 ms after the pull.

For the cores in crtgun_probe_cores (Model2A); LIGHTGUN_CRT_PROBE=0 turns it off.
The GUNDBG out trace gains pb_phase and pb_pressed and logs every 2 ms tick of a
probe sequence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
